      "text": "The batteries are changed every 5 months. To find the month they will be changed for the 25th time, we need to calculate the total number of months for 25 changes, then find out the month of the month 25 months after May.\n\n1. Calculate the total number of months:\n\\[\n25 \\text{ changes} \\times 5 \\text{ months per change} = 125 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\n2. Determine which month 125 months after May falls into. We know that each year has 12 months. Calculate how many complete years are in 125 months:\n\\[\n125 \\text{ months} \\div 12 \\text{ months/year} = 10 \\text{ years and } 5 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\n3. Since 10 years cover 10 complete years, we add these 10 years to May:\n\\[\nMay + 10 \\text{ years} = May + 10 \\times 12 \\text{ months} = May + 120 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\n4. Now, subtract the 5 extra months to find the month:\n\\[\nMay + 120 - 5 \\text{ months} = May + 115 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\n5. To find the month, determine the remainder of 115 months when divided by 12:\n\\[\n115 \\div 12 = 9 \\text{ R } 7 \\quad \\text{(Quotient: 9, Remainder: 7)}\n\\]\n\n6. The quotient tells us there are 9 full years, and the remainder of 7 months means the next year starts 7 months after May:\n\\[\nMay + 7 \\text{ months} = Dec\n\\]\n\nThus, the batteries will be changed for the 25th time in \\boxed{December}.",
